      "queue_bytes_high_water": 0,
      "pending_requests_high_water": 0,
      "fd_count": 0,
      "thread_count": 0,
      "task_high_water": 0
    },
    "missing_metrics": ["<a metric the workload did not report; it stays null, never 0>"],
    "notes": [
      "read_bytes/write_bytes come from the workload's own stage counters.",
      "allocated_bytes is a point-in-time allocator reading, not a peak; allocated_peak_bytes and peak_rss_bytes are the only peaks here.",
      "ab_perf.py does not emit allocated_peak_bytes or task_high_water: fill them from the soak report's allocator peak and background_tasks counter rather than leaving a 0 that reads as measured.",
      "rss_bytes is a macOS reading; it is never compared against a Linux pss_bytes.",
      "each side's peak is that process's own; peaks from separate processes are never summed.",
      "fd_count, thread_count and task_high_water come from the soak report (fd_count, thread_count, background_tasks), which samples them at quiescence."
    ]
  },
  "correctness": {
    "command": "<the suite that ran, e.g. cargo test --locked -p horon-agent-harness-api-server>",
